  #line-at(53.76pt, 287.52pt, "X-ray detected ferromagnetic resonance (XFMR) spectroscopy is an experimental technique for element-specific spin ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 299.52pt, "dynamics in the GHz regime and has been utilized to study spintronic materials. The XFMR signal is usually obtained ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 311.52pt, "by detecting X-ray excited optical luminescence (XEOL) emitted from a sample substrate. Here, we report the ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 323.52pt, "development of an XFMR spectrometer that is designed to place a photodetector for XEOL detection outside an ultra-")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 335.52pt, "high-vacuum chamber. This configuration allows for the easy replacement of detectors, such as photodiodes, CCD ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 347.52pt, "cameras, and spectrometers, depending on the experimental requirements. We demonstrated the measurement of ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 359.52pt, "XEOL spectra from MgO using a visible light spectrometer as well as the detection of XFMR signals originating from ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 371.52pt, "the spin precession of a permalloy (Ni")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(212.756pt, 372pt, "80")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.43pt, 371.52pt, "Fe")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(229.933pt, 372pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(236.606pt, 371.52pt, ") thin film using a photodiode detector. The XFMR spectrometer with an ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 383.52pt, "out-of-vacuum photodetector expands possibilities for advanced measurements such as XFMR microscopy. ")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.03pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(53.76pt, 407.372pt, "Keywords:")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(97.464pt, 407.52pt, " X-ray detected ferromagnetic resonance, X-ray magnetic circular dichroism, X-ray excited optical ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 419.52pt, "luminescence, spin precession, spin dynamics ")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.03pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(140.297pt, 442.412pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(67.26pt, 460.56pt, "In this era of information, the amount of electronic ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 472.56pt, "information is increasing rapidly. To process and store ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 484.56pt, "tremendous amounts of information in a sustainable ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 496.56pt, "manner, it is essential to improve the performance and ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 508.56pt, "energy efficiency of computing and storage devices. ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 520.56pt, "Spintronics is a promising technology that enables such ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 532.56pt, "advancements")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(113.433pt, 530.16pt, "1,2)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.772pt, 532.56pt, ". In addition to the electron charge ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 544.56pt, "degrees of freedom used in conventional electronics, ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 556.56pt, "spintronics also utilizes the electron spin degrees of ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 568.56pt, "freedom. Therefore, it is important to detect and control ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 580.56pt, "the electron spin. A wide range of materials are used in ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 592.56pt, "spintronic ")
  #line-at(114.361pt, 592.56pt, "devices, ")
  #line-at(165.471pt, 592.56pt, "including ")
  #line-at(223.073pt, 592.56pt, "ferromagnetic")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(281.225pt, 590.16pt, "3)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(286.56pt, 592.56pt, ", ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 604.56pt, "antiferromagnetic")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(128.757pt, 602.16pt, "4)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(134.092pt, 604.56pt, ", and ferrimagnetic")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(214.91pt, 602.16pt, "5)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(220.245pt, 604.56pt, ", as well as non-")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 616.56pt, "magnetic materials ranging from metals to insulators. ")
  #line-at(71.76pt, 628.56pt, "There are various experimental techniques for ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 640.56pt, "analyzing ")
  #line-at(104.914pt, 640.56pt, "magnetic ")
  #line-at(153.571pt, 640.56pt, "materials, ")
  #line-at(206.401pt, 640.56pt, "but ")
  #line-at(230.891pt, 640.56pt, "ferromagnetic ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 652.56pt, "resonance (FMR) is one of the most used. FMR measures ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 664.56pt, "the microwave absorption of a ferromagnetic sample ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 676.56pt, "placed in a static magnetic field. Recently, vector ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 688.56pt, "network analyzers (VNAs) have been widely utilized for ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 700.56pt, "FMR measurements")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(138.976pt, 698.16pt, "6)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(144.311pt, 700.56pt, ". By analyzing the FMR spectrum, ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 712.56pt, "magnetic properties such as effective magnetization, ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 442.56pt, "anisotropy, gyromagnetic ratio, damping, and exchange ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 454.56pt, "stiffness can be investigated. On the other hand, X-ray ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 466.56pt, "magnetic circular dichroism (XMCD) spectroscopy is a ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 478.56pt, "powerful experimental technique using synchrotron-")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 490.56pt, "radiation X-rays")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.671pt, 488.16pt, "7)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.006pt, 490.56pt, ". By tuning the energy of X-rays to the ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 502.56pt, "absorption edge of a specific element, element-selective ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 514.56pt, "magnetic measurements can be made. X-ray detected ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 526.56pt, "ferromagnetic ")
  #line-at(374.507pt, 526.56pt, "resonance ")
  #line-at(426.281pt, 526.56pt, "(XFMR) ")
  #line-at(469.74pt, 526.56pt, "is ")
  #line-at(486.865pt, 526.56pt, "a ")
  #line-at(502.038pt, 526.56pt, "combined ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 538.56pt, "technique of FMR and XMCD spectroscopy that enables ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 550.56pt, "element-specific analysis of spin precession dynamics")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(527.896pt, 548.16pt, "8)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(533.231pt, 550.56pt, ". ")
  #line-at(319.74pt, 562.56pt, "XFMR spectroscopy was demonstrated early this ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 574.56pt, "century ")
  #line-at(348.219pt, 574.56pt, "and ")
  #line-at(374.056pt, 574.56pt, "has ")
  #line-at(398.89pt, 574.56pt, "been ")
  #line-at(428.548pt, 574.56pt, "implemented ")
  #line-at(493.209pt, 574.56pt, "in ")
  #line-at(511.704pt, 574.56pt, "several ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 586.56pt, "synchrotron-radiation facilities")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(438.714pt, 584.16pt, "9–18)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(454.06pt, 586.56pt, ". This experimental ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 598.56pt, "technique has been applied to various kinds of magnetic ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 610.56pt, "systems such as single layer of films")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(462.026pt, 608.16pt, "9,11,19–21)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(494.053pt, 610.56pt, ", exchange-")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 622.56pt, "coupled bilayers")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.358pt, 620.16pt, "13,14,22–28)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(412.723pt, 622.56pt, ", and spin valves")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(493.579pt, 620.16pt, "29,30)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(510.592pt, 622.56pt, ". Spin-")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 634.56pt, "related phenomena such as spin pumping")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(480.919pt, 632.16pt, "31–38)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(499.602pt, 634.56pt, " and spin-")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 646.56pt, "transfer torque")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(370.028pt, 644.16pt, "39,40)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(387.041pt, 646.56pt, " have been observed. Leveraging the ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 658.56pt, "element-specific nature of XFMR, AC spin currents in ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 670.56pt, "non-magnetic ")
  #line-at(376.402pt, 670.56pt, "layers")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(401.727pt, 668.16pt, "41–43)")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(433.898pt, 670.56pt, "and ")
  #line-at(463.057pt, 670.56pt, "spin ")
