  #line-at(105.211pt, 533.04pt, "substrates ")
  #line-at(158.832pt, 533.04pt, "at ")
  #line-at(177.466pt, 533.04pt, "300")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(192.506pt, 533.04pt, "℃")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(210.771pt, 533.04pt, "using ")
  #line-at(243.729pt, 533.04pt, "magnetron ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 545.04pt, "sputtering. Two types of samples were prepared: (i) ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 557.04pt, "MgO(001)/Py(100 nm) and (ii) MgO(001)/Py(30 nm)/Cu(2 ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 569.04pt, "nm). A Cu capping layer was applied only to sample (ii) ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 581.04pt, "to prevent oxidation of the Py layer, whereas sample (i) ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 593.04pt, "was left uncapped to intentionally oxidize the Py film ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 605.04pt, "surface.  ")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.03pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.079pt, 628.892pt, "3. Details of the XFMR spectrometer")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(67.26pt, 647.04pt, "Schematic of the XFMR spectrometer is shown in Fig. ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 659.04pt, "1(b). The experimental system mainly consists of two ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 671.04pt, "parts. One is a microwave circuit that generates higher ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 683.04pt, "harmonics of a frequency of the master oscillator to apply ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 695.04pt, "RF magnetic field to a sample. It also controls time delay ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 707.04pt, "between RF signals and X-ray pulses. The other is a ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 719.04pt, "XEOL detection optics and detector system, which is ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 731.04pt, "connected to the data acquisition (DAQ) system of the ")
  #line-at(53.76pt, 743.04pt, "beamline. ")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.03pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(306.24pt, 75.212pt, "3.1 Microwave circuit")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(319.74pt, 87.36pt, "Figure 2(a) shows a block diagram of the microwave ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 99.36pt, "circuit used in the XFMR spectrometer. The master ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 111.36pt, "oscillator (MO) signal of the PF (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(447.478pt, 111.36pt, "𝑓")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(451.02pt, 113.28pt, "-$")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(459.37pt, 111.36pt, " = 500.1 MHz) was ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 123.36pt, "purified using a band-pass filter (F")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(450.959pt, 123.84pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(454.296pt, 123.36pt, ": 500 MHz band-pass ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 135.36pt, "filter, Mini-Circuits) and introduced to a delay line (DL: ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 147.36pt, "CDX-ATI011, Candox Systems Inc.) to control time delay ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 159.36pt, "between X-ray pulse and microwave signal into a ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 171.36pt, "coplanar waveguide (CPW). The delay line was driven by ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 183.36pt, "a motor driver (H718/GD-5410, Melec Inc.). Then, ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 195.36pt, "microwave signal was amplified by amplifier A")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(503.178pt, 195.84pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(506.515pt, 195.36pt, " to drive ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 207.36pt, "a comb generator (Comb: Model 7102, Picosecond Pulse ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 219.36pt, "Labs Inc.) which generates higher harmonics of the input ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 231.36pt, "signal. A suitable combination of band-pass, low-pass, ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 243.36pt, "and high-pass filters (F")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(403.538pt, 243.84pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(406.875pt, 243.36pt, ": Mini-Circuits) allowed only the ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 255.36pt, "3.5 GHz signal, which was used in this study, to pass ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 267.36pt, "through. Additional amplifiers (A")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(446.895pt, 267.84pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(450.231pt, 267.36pt, ": Mini-Circuits) and a ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 279.36pt, "programmable attenuator (Att: MN72A, Anritsu Co.) ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 291.36pt, "adjusted the power of the microwave signal. 3.5 GHz ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 303.36pt, "signal was introduced to CPW to generate RF magnetic ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 315.36pt, "field to drive spin precession in a sample. The ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 327.36pt, "transmitted ")
  #line-at(369.405pt, 327.36pt, "microwave ")
  #line-at(427.554pt, 327.36pt, "power ")
  #line-at(466.205pt, 327.36pt, "was ")
  #line-at(495.872pt, 327.36pt, "tuned ")
  #line-at(533.529pt, 327.36pt, "to ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 339.36pt, "approximately 20 dBm, as measured by a spectrum ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 351.36pt, "analyzer (SA: FSV SIGNAL ANALYZER, Rohde & ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 363.36pt, "Schwarz GmbH & Co. KG). ")
  #line-at(319.74pt, 375.36pt, "To generate the RF magnetic field at the sample ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 387.36pt, "position, we used a two-port CPW with 50-ohm ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 399.36pt, "characteristic impedance. The CPW was designed and ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 411.36pt, "fabricated by HAYASHI-REPIC Co., Ltd. (Tokyo, Japan), ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 423.36pt, "with a signal line width of 1 mm. A 0.5-mm-diameter ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 435.36pt, "pinhole was fabricated at the center of the signal line to ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 447.36pt, "allow ")
  #line-at(338.304pt, 447.36pt, "X-ray ")
  #line-at(371.351pt, 447.36pt, "transmission. ")
  #line-at(437.899pt, 447.36pt, "Figure ")
  #line-at(475.447pt, 447.36pt, "2(b) ")
  #line-at(501.338pt, 447.36pt, "shows ")
  #line-at(536.56pt, 447.36pt, "a ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 459.36pt, "photograph of the CPW with a sample in the XFMR ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 471.36pt, "measurement configuration. One port of signal line was ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 483.36pt, "connected to the RF signal generation system, which is ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 495.36pt, "described above, and another port was connected to the ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 507.36pt, "spectrum analyzer via SMA connectors. The sample, with ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 519.36pt, "its film side facing downward, was placed on the CPW so ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 531.36pt, "that it contacts the signal line, ensuring the effective ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 543.36pt, "application of the RF magnetic field. ")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.03pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(306.24pt, 567.212pt, "3.2 XEOL detection")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(319.74pt, 579.36pt, "Figure 3(a) shows a schematic of the XEOL detection ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 591.36pt, "system from a side view. X-ray impinges on the film side ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 603.36pt, "of the sample through a φ5-mm pinhole on the signal line ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 615.36pt, "of the CPW. X-rays that have transmitted through the ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 627.36pt, "film excite XEOL in the substrate near the film-substrate ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 639.36pt, "interface. XEOL is emitted isotropically into a 4π ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 651.36pt, "steradian solid angle and is collected by a plano-convex ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 663.36pt, "lens (uncoated N-BK7 plano-convex lens LA1951, ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 675.36pt, "Thorlabs Inc.) mounted on lens tubes (vacuum-")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 687.36pt, "compatible SM1 lens tubes, Thorlabs Inc.) for collimation. ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 699.36pt, "The collimated XEOL then passes through another ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 711.36pt, "plano-convex lens (uncoated N-BK7 plano-convex lens ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 723.36pt, "LA1131, Thorlabs Inc.) and is focused onto the light-")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 735.36pt, "receiving element of a photodetector through an ICF34 ")
  #line-at(306.24pt, 747.36pt, "viewport with borosilicate glass window. The detectable ")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.03pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(61.92pt, 360.572pt, "Fig. 2")
  #set text(font: "Century", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(87.635pt, 360.72pt, " (a) Block diagram of the microwave circuit. ")
  #line-at(61.92pt, 372.72pt, "Symbols indicate the master oscillator (MO), filters ")
